\\( k \\) such that \\( 0 \\leq k \\leq 1 \\).\n\nThis can be simplified to:\n\\[ P(x) = (1+k)x^2 - 2(1+k)x + (2+k) \\]\n\nWe are also given that \\( P(11) = 181 \\). Substituting \\( x = 11 \\) into the expression for \\( P(x) \\), we get:\n\\[ P(11) = (1+k)11^2 - 2(1+k)11 + (2+k) = 181 \\]\n\\[ (1+k)121 - 2(1+k)11 + (2+k) = 181 \\]\n\\[ 121 + 121k - 22 - 22k + 2 + k = 181 \\]\n\\[ 101 + 100k = 181 \\]\n\\[ 100k = 80 \\]\n\\[ k = \\frac{4}{5} \\]\n\nNow we substitute \\( k = \\frac{4}{5} \\) back into the expression for \\( P(x) \\):\n\\[ P(x) = \\left(1 + \\frac{4}{5}\\right)x^2 - 2\\left(1 + \\frac{4}{5}\\right)x + \\left(2 + \\frac{4}{5}\\right) \\]\n\\[ P(x) = \\frac{9}{5}x^2 - \\frac{18}{5}x + \\frac{14}{5} \\]\n\\[ P(x) = \\frac{9x^2 - 18x + 14}{5} \\]\n\nTo find \\( P(16) \\), we substitute \\( x = 16 \\) into the expression for \\( P(x) \\):\n\\[ P(16) = \\frac{9(16)^2 - 18(16) + 14}{5} \\]\n\\[ P(16) = \\frac{9 \\cdot 256 - 18 \\cdot 16 + 14}{5} \\]\n\\[ P(16) = \\frac{2304 - 288 + 14}{5} \\]\n\\[ P(16) = \\frac{2030}{5} \\]\n\\[ P(16) = 406 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( P(16) \\) is \\(\\boxed{406}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{406}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
